<p>French President Emmanuel Macron announced €23 billion, or about $27 billion, in investment commitments for Africa at the Africa Forward Summit in Nairobi, a two-day gathering co-hosted by Kenya and France on May 11-12. The package includes €14 billion from French public and private entities and €9 billion from African investors, with stated focus areas including energy transition, digital technology and AI, the maritime economy and agriculture. Kenyan President William Ruto called for an Africa-France partnership based on mutual respect, shared responsibility and investment rather than aid dependency, while Macron said the new relationship should be built around sovereignty and co-investment. The summit drew roughly 30 African heads of state and government and more than 3,000 delegates, according to reports from Nairobi. France held the meeting in Nairobi as Macron sought ties beyond Paris&#x27;s traditional francophone sphere; reports described Kenya as a strategic East African entry point. Macron also faced criticism after interrupting a summit panel to demand silence from audience members, saying they showed a &quot;total lack of respect&quot; during a presentation by artists and young entrepreneurs.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/MDKVqnHrvrdsQMWIO6EvTMk9yZwBf20mMazXz-2Aiv03BV6tpEe6-MHjmo919wB-Ytgy9evFajCS43vZ3eOec_uiRmzwmNs8T7nxIXFFtRsxBonzz9ya50bGpUQOGXntOdZXE28Sj_bsg1YxWnNl_LzZ2eS1CHyXVda_0V-gBxyeU1eAngR2poDzM_WgA05qnozXPP2jxMfxfDPySOS-zU8wSl0xPWbQ17ZjmmxUxx59PZbnR3sOerYVv6lrTJlU' alt='Emmanuel Macron addresses participants at the Africa Forward summit in Nairobi, Kenya, May 12, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Sector allocations: The French presidency listed €4.3 billion for energy transition, €3.76 billion for digital and AI, €3.3 billion for the blue economy, €1 billion for agriculture and €942 million for health.</li><li>Jobs target: Macron said the investment package would create 250,000 direct jobs in France and Africa.</li><li>Restitution push: Macron also highlighted new French legislation intended to ease the return of objects looted during the colonial era.</li><li>Peace focus: At the close of the summit, Macron called for &quot;African solutions&quot; for peace on the continent.</li></ul><blockquote>We are not simply here to come and invest on the African continent alongside you — we need the great African business leaders to come and invest in France - Emmanuel Macron</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>William Ruto: Kenya&#x27;s president urged governments and development partners after the summit to turn commitments into tangible progress, not leave them as summit declarations. (<a href='https://allafrica.com/stories/202605130075.html'>AllAfrica</a>)</li><li>Emmanuel Macron: Macron told The Africa Report before the summit that colonialism could no longer be blamed for all of Africa&#x27;s challenges, saying the decades after independence should not be exonerated from responsibility. (<a href='https://www.brecorder.com/news/40420744/macron-announces-23bn-euros-of-investment-at-africa-summit'>Business Recorder</a>)</li><li>António Guterres: The UN secretary-general said Africa demands investment at scale, justice in global systems and partnerships grounded in respect. (<a href='https://allafrica.com/stories/202605120697.html'>AllAfrica</a>)</li><li>Bola Tinubu: Nigeria&#x27;s president called for reform of the global financial architecture during the summit, placing financing rules at the center of Africa&#x27;s development agenda. (<a href='https://www.premiumtimesng.com/business/business-news/879086-at-africa-forward-summit-tinubu-calls-for-reform-of-global-financial-architecture.html'>Premium Times</a>)</li><li>French Foreign Minister Jean-Noël Barrot: Barrot said trade and investment between France and Africa far exceed Moscow&#x27;s involvement and said Russia had been largely defeated in Africa and elsewhere. (<a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/le-monde-africa/article/2026/05/13/french-foreign-minister-jean-noel-barrot-in-africa-as-elsewhere-in-the-world-russia-has-been-largely-defeated_6753383_124.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://japantoday.com/category/world/french-president-announces-billions-in-african-investments-at-summit-focused-on-partnership'>Macron unveils $27 billion investment in Africa at partnership summit in Kenya</a> - japantoday.com</li><li><a href='https://www.csmonitor.com/Editorials/the-monitors-view/2026/0512/Africa-refashions-relations-with-the-West'>Africa refashions relations with the West</a> - csmonitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/le-monde-africa/article/2026/05/13/french-foreign-minister-jean-noel-barrot-in-africa-as-elsewhere-in-the-world-russia-has-been-largely-defeated_6753383_124.html'>French Foreign Minister Jean-Noël Barrot: &#x27;In Africa, as elsewhere in the world, Russia has been largely defeated&#x27;</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/africa/article/3353386/french-presidents-onstage-outburst-kenya-overshadows-africa-bid'>French president’s onstage outburst in Kenya overshadows Africa bid</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/macron-faces-backlash-after-interrupting-africa-summit-panel-132908212'>Macron faces backlash after interrupting Africa summit panel in Kenya</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://allafrica.com/stories/202605130015.html'>Africa: Ruto Calls for Win-Win Africa-France Partnership At Nairobi Summit</a> - allafrica.com</li><li><a href='https://leadpakistan.com.pk/news/french-president-announces-billions-in-african-investments/'>French president announces billions in African investments</a> - leadpakistan.com.pk</li><li><a href='http://www.africanews.com/2026/05/12/africa-forward-summit-wraps-up-in-nairobi/'>Africa Forward summit wraps up in Nairobi</a> - africanews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theonlinekenyan.com/daily/2026-05-11/africa-forward-summi